        "* **Demographic Risk Factors:** I observed that the highest inconsistency and loss of customers occur between the ages of 40 and 60.While the bank maintains a young adult population (average age 39), this middle-aged segment shows a significant tendency to leave, suggesting a possible gap in long-term loyalty products.\n",
