        "id": "LFoLufZdU3J-"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 13. KMeans Clustering & Knee Detection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pYZRE_c3ViUh"
      },
      "source": [
        "I will now implement KMeans, a partitional clustering algorithm. KMeans effectively divides the space into regions similar to a Voronoi Diagram, where each customer is assigned to the nearest centroid.\n",
        "\n",
        "To avoid an arbitrary choice of K, I implement a geometric approach to identify the \"elbow\" of the inertia curve. By finding the optimal balance between group cohesion and the number of clusters, I ensure the segmentation is mathematically sound and avoids overfitting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "SadsXdCsVn83",
        "outputId": "c222c853-28f1-494d-a39d-7060d0fed47d"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "The optimal number of clusters according to the knee method is: K = 4\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def _knee_point(x, y):\n",
        "    # I convert data to numpy arrays for vectorized operations\n",
        "    x = np.array(list(x), dtype=float)\n",
        "    y = np.array(list(y), dtype=float)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Normalization to [0,1] to ensure different scales don't bias the geometry\n",
        "    x_n = (x - x.min()) / (x.max() - x.min() + 1e-12)\n",
        "    y_n = (y - y.min()) / (y.max() - y.min() + 1e-12)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # I define a line between the first and last point\n",
        "    p1 = np.array([x_n[0], y_n[0]])\n",
        "    p2 = np.array([x_n[-1], y_n[-1]])\n",
        "\n",
        "    line = p2 - p1\n",
        "    line = line / (np.linalg.norm(line) + 1e-12)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # I calculate the distance from each point to that line\n",
        "    pts = np.vstack([x_n, y_n]).T\n",
        "    vec = pts - p1\n",
        "    proj = vec @ line\n",
        "    proj_pts = np.outer(proj, line) + p1\n",
        "\n",
        "    # The \"knee\" is the point with the maximum distance to the line\n",
        "    dist = np.linalg.norm(pts - proj_pts, axis=1)\n",
        "    idx = int(np.argmax(dist))\n",
        "    return int(x[idx]), float(dist[idx])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Now I run KMeans for multiple values of K to generate the curve\n",
        "k_range = range(1, 11)\n",
        "inertia = []\n",
        "for k in k_range:\n",
        "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
        "    km.fit(X_scaled)\n",
        "    inertia.append(km.inertia_)\n",
        "\n",
        "# I call my function to find the optimal K\n",
        "k_opt, _ = _knee_point(k_range, inertia)\n",
        "\n",
