      "source": [
        "Unlike KMeans, DBSCAN doesn't require me to specify the number of clusters in advance. It identifies groups based on the density of points. This is particularly useful for detecting outliers (noise) and clusters with irregular shapes that traditional methods might miss. To configure it correctly, I will find the optimal epsilon (thTo complement the analysis, I implement DBSCAN. Unlike KMeans, this algorithm does not require a predefined number of clusters and is capable of identifying clusters of arbitrary shapes based on density.\n",
        "\n",
        "I use a K-distance plot to automatically determine the optimal Epsilon (Eps). This density-based approach is vital for detecting Noise (Outliers)—customers with unique behaviors that do not fit into any regular segment. This provides the bank with a robust tool to identify atypical financial profiles.e maximum distance between two samples for one to be considered as in the neighborhood of the other)."
